{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force","id":1028470,"title":"Musings on the Force","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T02:39:27-08:00","id":1028470,"title":"Musings on the Force","content":"This is just a random thread for the discussion of the Force from Star wars, mostly because I had an attack of philosophy yesterday, and ended up with what I thought was an interesting metaphor for the Light and the Dark sides.<br /> <br /> First, if we consider the power of the force - the actual exercise of force-powers - to be like water, I believe it can be said that the Light side is rather like a desert, while the Dark is more like an oily ocean. Let me explain.<br /> <br /> With the Light, the road to any kind of significant power is long and hard. Guides are needed, to show the way to the sparse oases. It requires great will and discipline to find one's way, but oh, the water is sweet! However, the further one journeys into the desert, the more one forgets the green of life and emotion and the more the sun burns away who you are, leaving a white, bleached and smooth thing where there was once a living being, a husk preaching the love, honor and nobility which it no longer understands and following the guiding light of the burning sun because it can no longer make a light of its own.<br /> <br /> With the Dark, claiming power requires only that you dip a cup over the side, but the power does not satisfy. It is bitter and salty, and leaves you craving more. All the while, one must be cautious that they do not fall from the boat and into the waters to drown. The waters are black and dark, and every draught stains the skin, the teeth and the tongue until the drinker is transfigured, unrecognisable to those who once knew him. Finally, the drinker is indistinguishable from the ocean from which he drank, more akin to an elemental force than a living, feeling, breathing thing, but godlike in his might and bestial in his endless hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-08-2017, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:36:52-08:00","id":1028670,"title":"","content":"That is a pretty cool metaphor. The only part where it breaks down for me is that it kind of treats the light side and the dark side as different forces - different waters, as it were. While this may or may not be the case in-setting, I have always preferred the philosophies that say the force is just the force, and light or dark is about how you use it.<br /> <br /> The Sith Academy on Korriban (no longer canon, but still a good source of insight) taught that the force is powered by emotion. Which if true would explain why the dark side is the easier route to greater force mastery. By letting yourself be ruled by your basest, most powerful emotions as the Sith do, you open the floodgates and channel the force with great ease. But by keeping careful control of all emotions as the Jedi do, you leave the well of force energy to dry, unless you continually dig deeper and deeper for a few more drops of moisture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:08:16-08:00","id":1028684,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine has an alternate theory on how midichlorians work that I've pretty much incorporated in my fanon. That they are a species of Force-sensitive and Force-attracted bacteria. Thus their relative concentration levels in a living being can be used as one (possible) indicator of their Force potential but they are not themselves the source of the Force in an individual nor is their concentration the only measure of someone's talent with the Force.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Qui Gonn's various pronouncements about them constitute a somewhat heretical view from Jedi orthodoxy, adding to the Jedi council's reticence to indulge his other unusual requests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 01-08-2017, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:28:21-08:00","id":1028693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028684#post1028684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine has an alternate theory on how midichlorians work that I've pretty much incorporated in my fanon. That they are a species of Force-sensitive and Force-attracted bacteria. Thus their relative concentration levels in a living being can be used as one (possible) indicator of their Force potential but they are not themselves the source of the Force in an individual nor is their concentration the only measure of someone's talent with the Force.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Qui Gonn's various pronouncements about them constitute a somewhat heretical view from Jedi orthodoxy, adding to the Jedi council's reticence to indulge his other unusual requests.</div> </div> </div> </div>So essentially a high midi-chlorian count is a byproduct of a strong force connection, instead of being the cause of said connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:02:10-08:00","id":1028703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028684#post1028684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine has an alternate theory on how midichlorians work that I've pretty much incorporated in my fanon. That they are a species of Force-sensitive and Force-attracted bacteria. Thus their relative concentration levels in a living being can be used as one (possible) indicator of their Force potential but they are not themselves the source of the Force in an individual nor is their concentration the only measure of someone's talent with the Force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this not how people usually view them? That was always the impression that I got from Qui-Gon's explanation. He said they are microscopic life forms in a symbiotic relationship, without which life could not exist and we would have no knowledge of the force, but never that they are the source of the force. In fact the phrasing, &quot;without them (...) we would have no knowledge of the force&quot; implies that the force would still exist without them, we just wouldn't know about it. Also we wouldn't exist... I assume there's an unspoken &quot;in the form that we know it now&quot; in there.<br /> <br /> Between that, and Lucas' confirmation that they're the Star Wars universe's rough anologue to mitochondria, it always just made sense to me that they are a form of force-sensitive organelle, and that the Jedi are aware of a correlation (but not necessarily a causation) between force sensitivity and high concentrations of midichlorians in the sensitive's cells. Qui Gon, as a strong believer in The Living Force, attributes his force sensitivity to those organelles &quot;whispering&quot; and &quot;telling him the will of the force&quot;, but that's clearly not how all Jedi view it.<br /> <br /> I'm also one of the few who was never bothered by the idea of midichlorians, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028684#post1028684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, Qui Gonn's various pronouncements about them constitute a somewhat heretical view from Jedi orthodoxy, adding to the Jedi council's reticence to indulge his other unusual requests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, as a believer in The Living Force, it makes sense that he would conceptualize the force in terms of symbiotic relationships. It's like... the Thyrsus' view of the force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-08-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:29:33-08:00","id":1028710,"title":"","content":"I had originally interpreted it as midichlorians acting as a 'channel' for the Force, an intermediary of sorts between the person and the actual Force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:00:43-08:00","id":1028726,"title":"","content":"I never really understood this, what is the Living Force and the Universal Force, I know it's an alternate axis to the Light/Dark you normally hear about. Is the Living Force the force of living things, and the universal the overall Force as a (near) omnipresent field, i.e. Force of beings vs. Force of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:51:22-08:00","id":1028758,"title":"","content":"My favorite Force musing was Darth Traya's in KotOR 2, where she took the idea of the Force and how it functioned to the logical conclusion that was an omniscient, omnipotent, wicked, and malevolent god-being that needed to be destroyed and was frustrated by the fact that destroying something which is omnipotent and omniscient is simply impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:06:20-08:00","id":1028771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028726#post1028726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really understood this, what is the Living Force and the Universal Force, I know it's an alternate axis to the Light/Dark you normally hear about. Is the Living Force the force of living things, and the universal the overall Force as a (near) omnipresent field, i.e. Force of beings vs. Force of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Living Force and The Unifying Force are differing views on what the force <i>is</i>. Most Jedi subscribe to the Living Force philosophy, which says that the force is a sort of energy that exists within all living things. It also says that the force has dual aspects, commonly referred to as the light side and the dark side. Conversely, the Unifying Force view is less popular among the Jedi, says that the force is a single, conscious entity, with no light and dark side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:07:48-08:00","id":1028772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028758#post1028758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite Force musing was Darth Traya's in KotOR 2, where she took the idea of the Force and how it functioned to the logical conclusion that was an omniscient, omnipotent, wicked, and malevolent god-being that needed to be destroyed and was frustrated by the fact that destroying something which is omnipotent and omniscient is simply impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Traya is an example of an extremist interpretation of Unifying Force philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:27:15-08:00","id":1028812,"title":"","content":"Here's something I've always found to be a hot point of debate. Darth Bane instituted the Rule of Two in part because he believed there were too many Sith and that was causing their power to diminish as they overdraw the well of the Force. Some people I've discussed this with don't believe this is possible due to the Force being generated by all living things in the universe and therefore impossible for even hundreds of thousands or millions of Force users to deplete its strength. Others have posited it might imply that while the Force is infinite in scope it has only so much ambient presence in a given system or galaxy that be drawn upon at once. What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:08:25-08:00","id":1028827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028812#post1028812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That being a force-user is more about belief and cultivation than science.<br /> <br /> Taking a Watsonian perspective on all the different ways the Force has been presented by different writers, I posit that <i>nobody</i> really has a complete understanding of what the Force is or how it works. Different people find different ways to manipulate it, drawing on such things as extreme emotion, highly focused discipline, or empathetic symbiosis as means of gaining power. Some of them form schools that manage to persist for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Darth Bane might be completely wrong about the force being limited, or not. What really matters is that <i>he think</i><i>s</i> he is correct, and is able to persuade others to follow suit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-09-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:35:16-08:00","id":1028852,"title":"","content":"It always seemed more likely that Darth Bane was completely bonkers than he was right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:37:11-08:00","id":1028853,"title":"","content":"I thought Bane instituted the Rule of Two to put a stop to the infighting among the Sith and to insure the Mantle Dark Lord of the Sith would always belong to the most powerful among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:27:09-08:00","id":1028865,"title":"","content":"I mean yeah, the mantle of the Dark Lord of the Sith would always belong to the most powerful Sith but that was because after Bane there was often only one Sith (or two if he had an apprentice) so that Sith would by default be the &quot;strongest&quot; Sith. It's kind of like me bragging about how I'm the most powerful person in my apartment - once you realize there's nobody else in my apartment but me, it's maybe not quite so impressive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:41:13-08:00","id":1028870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028865#post1028865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean yeah, the mantle of the Dark Lord of the Sith would always belong to the most powerful Sith but that was because after Bane there was often only one Sith (or two if he had an apprentice) so that Sith would by default be the &quot;strongest&quot; Sith. It's kind of like me bragging about how I'm the most powerful person in my apartment - once you realize there's nobody else in my apartment but me, it's maybe not quite so impressive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if you got a roommate and trained them until they became powerful enough to kick you out of the apartment, and then they got a new roommate and trained them the same, you would ensure that the sole apartment occupant was continually getting more powerful with each cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T22:20:04-08:00","id":1028879,"title":"","content":"The problem was, it didn't really work out like that - it would be one thing if the Sith were murdering one another at the height of their power, but that's not usually what would happen. Rather the apprentice would wait until the more powerful sith started to grow older and weaker and then the younger one would kill him. <br /> <br /> So if you think of it as a &quot;power rating&quot; scale, a Sith might hit 100, slowly grow weaker and get killed by their apprentice once they're at a 70 - so the apprentice is maybe a 75. He trains, hits 100, grows weaker and then gets killed by his apprentice.<br /> <br /> It's one of those things I don't think Darth Bane really thought through very well... but then like I said, he was kind of bonkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:25:40-08:00","id":1029046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028853#post1028853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Bane instituted the Rule of Two to put a stop to the infighting among the Sith and to insure the Mantle Dark Lord of the Sith would always belong to the most powerful among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also that, hence why I said &quot;in part.&quot; The two main reasons were the reason I mentioned about his belief that their Force abilities were being diminished by their numbers and the reason you mention about his perception that the title of Sith Lord was being debased by too many aspirants, sycophants, and paranoids fighting among themselves.<br /> <br /> So thenceforth there would be only two. No more, no less. Except for the secret backup apprentice. And the apprentice's secret apprentice. And the various guys who kind of dark side trained but not really in the org chart. Two though. That's what I'm getting at. Just two. Definitely just two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:34:31-08:00","id":1029051,"title":"","content":"True. And yet against all logic it did work out well for the Sith until they started ignoring it. Sideous conquored the whole galaxy. Then he discarded the Rule of Two and created his own Rule of One and got himself killed by his redeemed apprentice, completely breaking the cycle and leading to the downfall of one of the greatest Sith-ruled empires in centuries. So, maybe it was just luck that the Rule of Two served the Sith well and that abandoning it lead to their downfall again. But as Kenobi said, in his experience there's no such thing as luck. Maybe Bane was onto something. Maybe it's the will of the Unifying Force orce that there be two Sith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:57:30-08:00","id":1029066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1028670#post1028670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a pretty cool metaphor. The only part where it breaks down for me is that it kind of treats the light side and the dark side as different forces - different waters, as it were. While this may or may not be the case in-setting, I have always preferred the philosophies that say the force is just the force, and light or dark is about how you use it.<br /> <br /> The Sith Academy on Korriban (no longer canon, but still a good source of insight) taught that the force is powered by emotion. Which if true would explain why the dark side is the easier route to greater force mastery. By letting yourself be ruled by your basest, most powerful emotions as the Sith do, you open the floodgates and channel the force with great ease. But by keeping careful control of all emotions as the Jedi do, you leave the well of force energy to dry, unless you continually dig deeper and deeper for a few more drops of moisture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the rest of the thread yet, but I love this and completely agree. I believe it HAS been recanonized that not everyone does ascribe to the philosophy of The Living Force (including Palpatine), which I like very much. I'm not especially interested in those black and white questions, I'm a lot more interested in the actions people take and why we should characterize them as good and evil based on those actions. For example, obviously, Anakin murdering all of those children was disgusting and horrific and terrible. The Jedi Order using slave labor to power the GAR was also disgusting and horrific and terrible, and I typically think of the Jedi Order labeling themselves as &quot;good&quot; and following the &quot;light&quot;, to dismiss any sort of criticism about their behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:44:11-08:00","id":1029151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029051#post1029051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. And yet against all logic it did work out well for the Sith until they started ignoring it. Sideous conquored the whole galaxy. Then he discarded the Rule of Two and created his own Rule of One and got himself killed by his redeemed apprentice, completely breaking the cycle and leading to the downfall of one of the greatest Sith-ruled empires in centuries. So, maybe it was just luck that the Rule of Two served the Sith well and that abandoning it lead to their downfall again. But as Kenobi said, in his experience there's no such thing as luck. Maybe Bane was onto something. Maybe it's the will of the Unifying Force orce that there be two Sith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I subscribe to the theory that if the Force has a &quot;will&quot; at all it isn't one that neatly conforms to the Light/Dark dichotomy and that its long arc has been towards the destruction of both the Jedi and Sith as organizing principles. In my view Anakin Skywalker indeed fulfilled the prophecy of the chosen one and brought balance to the Force by destroying both the Jedi and the Sith traditions. Luke is technically a Jedi by his own assertion and training, but he lacks the rigid orthodoxy and dogma of the old Jedi Order and his victory grew out of simultaneously accepting and rejecting basic tenets of Jedi philosophy. Thus the Force was given a new beginning, at last freed from the cycle imposed upon it by the two dominant traditions of Force users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:12:17-08:00","id":1029163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029151#post1029151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I subscribe to the theory that if the Force has a &amp;quot;will&amp;quot; at all it isn't one that neatly conforms to the Light/Dark dichotomy and that its long arc has been towards the destruction of both the Jedi and Sith as organizing principles. In my view Anakin Skywalker indeed fulfilled the prophecy of the chosen one and brought balance to the Force by destroying both the Jedi and the Sith traditions. Luke is technically a Jedi by his own assertion and training, but he lacks the rigid orthodoxy and dogma of the old Jedi Order and his victory grew out of simultaneously accepting and rejecting basic tenets of Jedi philosophy. Thus the Force was given a new beginning, at last freed from the cycle imposed upon it by the two dominant traditions of Force users.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I fully agree with that intepretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:29:46-08:00","id":1029232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029151#post1029151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I subscribe to the theory that if the Force has a &quot;will&quot; at all it isn't one that neatly conforms to the Light/Dark dichotomy and that its long arc has been towards the destruction of both the Jedi and Sith as organizing principles. In my view Anakin Skywalker indeed fulfilled the prophecy of the chosen one and brought balance to the Force by destroying both the Jedi and the Sith traditions. Luke is technically a Jedi by his own assertion and training, but he lacks the rigid orthodoxy and dogma of the old Jedi Order and his victory grew out of simultaneously accepting and rejecting basic tenets of Jedi philosophy. Thus the Force was given a new beginning, at last freed from the cycle imposed upon it by the two dominant traditions of Force users.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all it cost was two horrific intergalactic wars and the near genocide of an entire religious/peacekeeping organization.<br /> <br /> The Force works in mysterious ways, I guess.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the Force isn't alive or sentient in anyway we would understand. There's also probably no Light side or Dark side. To me it's just a Tool that connects and corespondents to random people's Will and Desires allowing said people to achieve what they want through single-minded Willpower*. That's why the Jedi were so obsessed with getting rid of distracting temptations and desires that might lead a Padawan's Focus away from the organization's singular purpose of ensuring peace in the Republic. A fractured Will results in a weakened and divided connection to the Force, just look at Kylo Ren and his temptation to the &quot;Light&quot; and his family as an example of this. The Sith get this as well and just replace the Jedi's singular Focus of &quot;protecting the Republic&quot; with a singular Focus of getting power, and perhaps more importantly freedom**, throwing all other concerns like empathy for others and intergalactic peace to the wayside on account of their distracting nature. That's why dogmatic traditions like the Jedi, the Sith, the Imperial Knights and even the Grey Jedi to some extent exist. Scatter-brained ideologies that don't Focus on a singular pursuit be it Wisdom, Power, Peace, Freedom, etc just don't result in strong Force users. The fractured self is a weakened self in essence.<br /> <br /> * So, yeah, I think they're basically less powerful Mages Ascension-style.<br /> <br /> ** Actually the Sith have a real interesting philosophy in that I don't think domination of others is their primary goal. I think building an authoritarian Sith Empire is just a step towards their real goal of achieving completely unfettered freedom from everyone and everything, including death. In the end goal any true Sith to me should be narcissistic apotheosis and perhaps even solipsism.<br /> <br /> My chains are broken, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 01-09-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:39:49-08:00","id":1029235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029232#post1029232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And all it cost was two horrific intergalactic wars and the near genocide of an entire religious/peacekeeping organization.<br /> <br /> The Force works in mysterious ways, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody ever said the will of the Force mapped to an objective moral good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:41:40-08:00","id":1029238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029232#post1029232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And all it cost was two horrific intergalactic wars and the near genocide of an entire religious/peacekeeping organization.<br /> <br /> The Force works in mysterious ways, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm much more interested in discussing the Empire's abuses around designating trillions of beings as nonsentient so as to enslave them.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, they massacred the Jedi Order, but the Jedi were also genocidally minded when it came to the Sith, both the Sith species and the Sith Order.<br /> <br /> They were both genocidal, abusive and institutional powers. I'm not trying to justify Palpatine's genocide, but let's not talk about the Jedi like perfect unicorns. They used slave labor. They did plenty of horrific shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:51:07-08:00","id":1029273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029238#post1029238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm much more interested in discussing the Empire's abuses around designating trillions of beings as nonsentient so as to enslave them.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, they massacred the Jedi Order, but the Jedi were also genocidally minded when it came to the Sith, both the Sith species and the Sith Order.<br /> <br /> They were both genocidal, abusive and institutional powers. I'm not trying to justify Palpatine's genocide, but let's not talk about the Jedi like perfect unicorns. They used slave labor. They did plenty of horrific shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say that the Jedi were perfect unicorns? No I don't think I did. Besides, the Jedi are more like sage mountain goats.<br /> <br /> Also, I was commenting on the idea the Force &quot;willing&quot; the destruction of the Jedi and Sith probably wasn't worth the Clone Wars and the Galactic Civil War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:58:49-08:00","id":1029277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029273#post1029273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I say that the Jedi were perfect unicorns? No I don't think I did. Besides, the Jedi are more like sage mountain goats.<br /> <br /> Also, I was commenting on the idea the Force &quot;willing&quot; the destruction of the Jedi and Sith probably wasn't worth the Clone Wars and the Galactic Civil War.</div> </div> </div> </div>...don't know why this is getting so tense. I never said &quot;Weirdboyz said the Jedi are perfect unicorns, wow, what a stupid comment&quot;, because that's not what I was saying, and it wasn't personal. I didn't even use the words &quot;you shouldn't say&quot;. It was a general comment. I didn't snap at you. Please don't snap at me either. It seems we're agreeing entirely, if you what you were saying is &quot;the Force &quot;willing&quot; the destruction of the Jedi and Sith probably wasn't worth the Clone Wars and the Galactic Civil War,&quot; so I don't much understand where the conversation has gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T15:04:26-08:00","id":1029279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1029235#post1029235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody ever said the will of the Force mapped to an objective moral good.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why should it map towards a desire to destroy rigid ideologies? Why would the Force even care about that? Hell, if Luke was supposed to a glorious new beginning for Force-education freed from religious dogma, why did it allow Kylo Ren to destroy Luke's fancy new Order?<br /> <br /> It makes sense to me that the Force has no will or desire whatsoever and instead just empowers anyone who does. The original Jedi Order fell because Sheev really, really desired them to fall and worked really, really worked hard to accomplish it. The reason why the Sith fell is because Anakin really, really didn't want to see his son tortured anymore. They had willed things to happen and through the empowerment of the Force and their own actions it happened. Even the prophecy seems unless like the Force giving the Jedi subtle notice of its future plans and more like some random Jedi Seer being decent at their job.<br /> <br /> But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:36:32-08:00","id":1029374,"title":"","content":"Canon has a the Force having two axi. The dark/light and living/cosmic, which is similiar but different to the EU's Unifying/living split.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:37:31-08:00","id":1034589,"title":"","content":"Just a thought: If the usage of the Force requires will - which I think it can be safely said that it does - and that power scales with will - a slightly shakier assumption -, could it be said that the reason that the Sith tend to be more personally powerful than Jedi is because their will to affect change in the world is fuelled by their emotions, their feelings and their desires, while the power of Jedi and 'light-side' traditions usually relies upon will produced 'ex nihilo', which is used to enforce the results of reasoned thought and 'wisdom'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:36:52-08:00","id":1034704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1034589#post1034589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought: If the usage of the Force requires will - which I think it can be safely said that it does - and that power scales with will - a slightly shakier assumption -, could it be said that the reason that the Sith tend to be more personally powerful than Jedi is because their will to affect change in the world is fuelled by their emotions, their feelings and their desires, while the power of Jedi and 'light-side' traditions usually relies upon will produced 'ex nihilo', which is used to enforce the results of reasoned thought and 'wisdom'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is very true. It's also why Jedi become so powerful when they don't completely eschew emotion, like with Mace Windu's Vaapad. Emotion is natural and normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:57:16-08:00","id":1034720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1028470-musings-on-the-force?p=1034704#post1034704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is very true. It's also why Jedi become so powerful when they don't completely eschew emotion, like with Mace Windu's Vaapad. Emotion is natural and normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmhmm. On the other hand, giving in completely to emotion and wallowing in ones' every passion, as the Sith do, is an excellent way to drive oneself mad with conflicting emotions. Also, I think it bears mention that many of the Jedi focus not so much on using the Force directly, but rather on divining its will and acting it out. In that sense, emptying yourself so as to reduce distraction from the Force's subtle currents is a good strategy, albeit one that comes at a hefty price for - at least from my perspective - comparatively little gain. On the other hand, the Jedi are essentially a religion dedicated to the Force itself (or the light side, at least), it is possible that they see communion with the Force as an end in and of itself. I myself find that idea a little hard to grasp, but that may simply due to my attitude towards seeking solace and aid from a nebulous 'higher power' (apologies to any I might offend by that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}